**Company Description**
 Eurofins Scientific is an international life sciences company which provides a unique range of analytical testing services to clients across multiple industries. The Group believes it is the world leader in food, environment and pharmaceutical products testing and in agroscience CRO services. It is also one of the global independent market leaders in certain testing and laboratory services for genomics, discovery pharmacology, forensics, advanced material sciences and for supporting clinical studies. In addition, Eurofins is one of the key emerging players in specialty clinical diagnostic testing in Europe and the USA.




 Group's key figures are approx. 7\.296 billion Euros turnover, over 950 laboratories across 59 countries and about 65,000 staff.




**Job Description**
**Job description:**
* Act as a functional expert to collect, challenge and agree on business requirements for digitalizing business processes;
* Translate business requirements/processes into functional specifications and give detailed judgement on business complexity to promote simplification;
* Act as a product owner for the business processes and be responsible for the communication and cooperation between business and IT development teams;
* Write and maintain best practice documentation and train administrators and key users;
* Ensure level 2 support during transition life cycle (deployment) and level 3 support during operational life cycle;
* Audit and review use of the new tools to ensure implementation of best practice processes;
* Model the requirements into user stories (work items for development team) with the appropriate set of artefacts.


**EVOLUTION:** 
*(for publication on Eurofins website and career portals)*
**What We Offer**
* The opportunity to grow your functional analysis skills in a demanding, fast growing organization.
* A chance to become part of an international team of professionals, working on a strategic and highly visible program.


**QUALIFICATIONS AND EXPERIENCE REQUIRED:** 
*(maximum 500 characters (not including spaces) for short position posting and for posting on Eurofins website and career portals)*
**Profile Description**
* Self\-motivated, professional team player with customer focus;
* Affinity with and good understanding of IT concepts and digital technologies;
* Attention to detail, assertive.
* University degree in Business Engineering, Computer Science or similar educational background;
* Efficient time management and high quality attitude;
* Experience in agile development methods (scrum), preferably using Azure DevOps;
* Preferable: experience with workflows and related IT solutions.


**Qualifications**
**Requirements:**
* 6\+ years of experience in analysing, describing and challenging processes and workflows;
* Knowledge of UML and other tool to create diagrams, tools to create wireframes
* Master’s degree in business administration / commercial sciences / computer sciences;
* Excellent analytical and problem solving skills;
* Excellent English language skills;
* Knowledge of service oriented software architecture;


 Excellent verbal/written communication skills

**About the School of Human Development (SHD)** 




 The School of Human Development (SHD) at IIHS focuses on social transformation. The




 School understands social transformation as a set of processes that are rooted in, and seek to




 directly address:



1. Inequality in social status and substantive rights based on identity;
2. The absence of material and economic dignity for the urban majority; and
3. Inequities in political presence, recognition and participation.



 The School’s core focus areas are:



* Decent work;
* Affordable housing;
* Social inequality;
* Social protection;
* Urban health;
* Community mobilization;
* Care Infrastructure.









**Job Description** 




 IIHS is seeking an experienced candidate to primarily support research on housing policy, with




 a specific focus on rental housing and senior housing. The consultant will contribute to




 evidence\-based research, data analysis, and field investigations that inform policy




 recommendations and programme design in these areas. Additionally, they will assist with




 research work related to economic geography mapping.










 This will be a contractual position for an initial term of 11 months, renewable on mutual




 consent.










**Activities and Tasks** 




 Responsibilities would include, but not be limited to, the following:



* Conducting in\-depth research on housing policy issues, with emphasis on rental housing and senior/ elderly housing segments;
* Designing and carrying out fieldwork, including primary data collection, site visits, and stakeholder consultations;
* Collecting, organising, and analysing real estate and housing market data from diverse sources (government, industry, and primary data);
* Developing financial and policy models in Excel to support analysis and scenario planning;
* Reviewing existing and future housing policies, regulatory frameworks, and best practices, related to regional economic geography development, including relevant national and international case studies;
* Preparing well\-structured reports, briefs, presentations, and other knowledge products summarising research findings;
* Participating in teaching the “Practica” (field \- based interdisciplinary studio) for Masters students at IIHS;
* Collaborating with internal teams, government stakeholders, and external partners as required;
* Providing inputs and recommendations to strengthen rental and senior housing policy and programming;
* Carrying out the administrative work that supports the primary and additional requirements;
* Providing support to other IIHS activities including academics, research, training, practice, operations and others;
* Participating in all activities of Institution\-Building at IIHS; carrying out tasks as assigned by IIHS; and traveling on IIHS work within or outside the country as and when needed.









**Structure and Reporting** 




 The incumbent will be an External Consultant coordinating with the Lead \- Research at IIHS




 and will be required to collaborate effectively with a diverse group of internal teams and




 external individuals/ organisations, and students.










**Person Specification** 




 The ideal candidate should have:



* A minimum of 5 years of relevant work experience after a Master's degree in Planning, Economics, Architecture, Real Estate, or a related field; or a minimum of 7 years of relevant work experience on issues related to Housing, Real Estate, and Planning with or without a Bachelor’s degree;
* Demonstrated experience in conducting fieldwork, including data collection and stakeholder engagement;
* Strong understanding of different types of real estate data and data sources;
* Strong understanding of economic/ spatial planning methods;
* Proficiency in Excel, including financial/ data modelling;
* Strong analytical, research, and report\-writing skills;
* The ability to work independently and guide researchers, and students in the Practica;
* The ability to manage timelines in a consulting environment.
* Prior experience in a consulting role, preferably in management, policy, or real estate consulting;
* A background in community development, affordable housing, or rental housing programmes;
* Experience with teaching will be valued.









 This is a contractual engagement for an initial term of 11 months, renewable on




 mutual consent. This offer is on an exclusive basis, which implies that other professional




 assignments (whether compensated or not) that bear a potential conflict of interest with IIHS




 cannot be undertaken.










 The search will remain open until the position is filled.










**Location** 




 This position is based in Bengaluru and may entail travel to other locations in India.










**Review and Assessment** 




 The role and performance of the incumbent shall be subject to normal review and




 assessment systems at IIHS.










**Diversity Policy** 




 IIHS is an equal opportunity employer that encourages women, people with disabilities and




 those from economically and socially excluded communities with the requisite skills and




 qualifications to apply for positions.










 Contact




 Please write to us at careers@iihs.co.in if you need any clarifications while filling the online




 application form.
